## Cost: paracetamol (20 atoms, 199 AOs), wB97M-V/def2-SVP, (99,590)/(50,194): 642472 XC points, 131384 VV10 points
## (hess_grid_response_parts.py, one process; the laptop drifts 10-20% between runs, so A/B of whole Hessians is noisy)
grid_response=False: XC energy grid terms -,      VV10 energy 28-32 s, make_h1 88-89 s
grid_response=True:  XC energy grid terms 27-30 s, VV10 energy 77-83 s, make_h1 104-111 s (max_memory 4000: the VV10
                     pair terms not kept), 70 s with max_memory 12000 (kept from the energy terms)
=> about +60 s on a ~350 s Hessian (+17%) when the VV10 pair terms fit in memory (6 x natm*3 x VV10 points doubles)
Whole Hessian (verbose 5 timers, max_memory 4000): 335 -> 475 s with the first numpy version; 348 -> 499 s with the
C kernels but the VV10 pair terms not kept (memory), CPHF 199 -> 240 s at the same 4 cycles / 224-226 vectors (drift).
